# Security module

**Read the full memory model first:** [`.cursor/rules/docs/security-module.md`](docs/security-module.md)

User & Security admin APIs live in `backend/src/security/`. Auth login/logout/refresh/me/change-password/change-required-password stay in `backend/src/auth/`.

## Golden rules

1. **Reads** use `prisma.client`; **writes** use `unitOfWork.run` only.
2. **All mutations** — audit + outbox in the same transaction (`AuditModule.SECURITY`).
3. **Org-global** — no branch scoping on list/get (except session records carry `branchId` from login).
4. **Nested junctions** — parent FK from **route param** (`userId`, `roleId`), not create body.
5. **Never expose** `passwordHash` in API responses.
6. **Invalidate sessions** on user deactivate, password reset, role/permission changes.

## Lifecycle (no workflows)

| Rule | Where |
|------|-------|
| Soft delete | `deletedAt`; filter `deletedAt: null` |
| Optimistic lock | `version` on update/delete; `optimisticUpdate()` |
| Role delete | Block if `userRoles` exist (`ROLE_IN_USE`) |
| Permission delete | Block if `rolePermissions` exist (`PERMISSION_IN_USE`) |
| User create | `employeeId` FK validation only; hash password via `PasswordService` |
| Junction replace | `PUT .../replace` — soft-delete removed, upsert new; invalidate sessions |

## Layer checklist

- **DTOs:** update requires `version`; nested create has parent FK from route only.
- **Mappers:** one-way `to{Entity}Response()`; IDs as strings; never map `passwordHash`.
- **Services:** `assertUserExists` / `assertRoleExists` for nested routes.
- **Permissions:** `SECURITY:RESOURCE:ACTION` on every endpoint (`@RequirePermissions`).
- **Constants:** [`security.constants.ts`](../backend/src/security/constants/security.constants.ts) — `LogoutReason`.
- **Utils:** [`security.util.ts`](../backend/src/security/utils/security.util.ts), [`session.util.ts`](../backend/src/security/utils/session.util.ts).

## Not implemented

Unit/persistence/e2e tests, Angular clients, MFA, password policy settings.

